<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/undated">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ottoman–Habsburg wars</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ottoman-Habsburg rivalry</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ottoman–<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> wars were a long series of conflicts between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> and the Habsburg monarchy, fought from the sixteenth to the eighteenth century in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>. They included the sieges of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> in 1529 and 1683. The rivalry structured European geopolitics and alliances from the 1520s through the late seventeenth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ottoman-habsburg-wars.jpg" alt="Ottoman–Habsburg wars" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Elanoraga · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MixCollage-15-Jan-2024-09-37-PM-7066.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
